## Fix
1. **Position beats length.** search() first commits to the LEFTMOST starting
   position that can produce a complete match — this happens BEFORE greediness is
   considered. Greedy/lazy only decides HOW MUCH is consumed at that already-chosen
   position; it never lets a shorter match further right win over an earlier one.

2. **Greedy vs lazy is a preference, settled by backtracking.**
   - greedy '.*'  : grab as much as possible, then RELEASE chars one at a time if
                    the rest of the pattern fails (backtrack = move backward).
   - lazy   '.*?' : grab as little as possible, then CONSUME chars one at a time if
                    the rest of the pattern fails (backtrack = advance, but each
                    advance is CAUSED by a failed check rewinding to the quantifier).
   Both are the same mechanism: on failure, return to the last quantifier with
   untried options and try its next amount.
